\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Dear Mr Avbunudje,\
\
We have reviewed your DSA application and I am pleased to confirm that as your study needs have not changed your DSA will continue as per your most recent support letter.\
\
For further academic years you will only need to apply every academic year on a DSA full form for DSA if you:\
\
\'a0 \'a0- \'a0 \'a0are a postgraduate student\
\'a0 \'a0- \'a0 \'a0are a part-time student\
\'a0 \'a0- \'a0 \'a0only get DSA funding (i.e. no tuition fees/maintenance loan etc.)\
\
You do not need to provide medical evidence or ID every year if you are continuing on the same course at the same university or college. \
\
We will also require an application if you:\
\
\'a0 \'a0- \'a0 \'a0are changing course \
\'a0 \'a0- \'a0 \'a0are changing university or college\
\'a0 \'a0- \'a0 \'a0are repeating a year of study\
\
If you have any queries about this support or you feel further recommendations are required you must contact your Disability Adviser at your university or college.\
\
For further information about DSA go to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "www.gov.uk/studentfinance"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 www.gov.uk/studentfinance}}, call us on 0300 100 0607 or email us at dsa_team@slc.co.uk.\
\
Yours sincerely,\
\
\
Anoop Ghundoo | On Behalf of the DSA Team\
Student Loans Company\
Memphis Building, Lingfield Point, Darlington DL1 1RW\
